#> tool: sedrepl
#> wait: mAN
#> pause: 50
#> must: In Xanadu did Kubla Khan
#> must: Where Alph, the sacred river, rAN
#> must: Through caverns measureless to mAN
#> not: KhAN
#> not: XAN
#> source: b end
# 19. Flow of control: labels, b and t. McMahon 3.6
# :name marks a place; b name jumps there (b alone: to the end of the script).
# t name jumps only if an s has substituted since the last input line or the
# last t. The loop replaces one "an" per pass until none is left, like the g
# flag. Line 1 never enters it: /Kubla/b end jumps over, so it is unchanged.
# Try: delete the /Kubla/ line: now line 1 is changed twice.
/Kubla/b end
:again
s/an/AN/
t again
:end

#DATA
In Xanadu did Kubla Khan
A stately pleasure dome decree:
Where Alph, the sacred river, ran
Through caverns measureless to man
Down to a sunless sea.
